<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  launchd job description for Sentry's own Mach service - the XPC endpoint
  the bundled `macstat` CLI and `MacStatMCP` stdio binary connect to.
  Installed into Sentry.app/Contents/Library/LaunchAgents/ and registered by
  `SMAppService.agent(plistName:)` from `MCPAgentRegistrar`, only when the
  user explicitly asks for it in Settings > AI Access > Command-Line Access.

  THE FILE NAME IS PART OF THE API, same rule as the fan daemon's plist one
  directory over in the built bundle: `SMAppService.agent(plistName:)` looks
  this file up by basename inside Contents/Library/LaunchAgents, launchd
  requires `Label` to equal that basename minus ".plist", and here the Mach
  service name is deliberately the SAME string again, so label, basename and
  service name cannot drift apart. All three come from `MCPAgentNaming`,
  and `MCPAgentRegistrationTests` pins the exact text.

  WHY THE PROGRAM IS THE APP ITSELF. The listener for this service lives in
  `AppDelegate` (`startMCPListener`), because the service's implementation -
  `MCPXPCService` - needs the app's live object graph: StatsCoordinator,
  HistoryStore, the access controller, all of it. A separate helper binary
  would need its own copy of that state or a second hop back into the app.
  So the agent's BundleProgram is the app binary, which means: when a client
  connects and Sentry isn't running, launchd LAUNCHES SENTRY - menu bar
  icon and all. That is the designed behavior, not an accident: the CLI's
  whole promise is "ask this Mac about itself", and an answer requires the
  process that has the answers.

  WHAT IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT

  RunAtLoad / KeepAlive
      Omitted, so both default to false. Whether Sentry opens at login is
      the user's call via the existing login-item mechanism, not something
      this plist smuggles in; registering command-line access must not
      also mean "and Sentry now autostarts". launchd starts the app on
      demand when a client connects, and never resurrects it after quit.

  LimitLoadToSessionType
      Omitted; the default (Aqua) is exactly right for a job whose program
      is a GUI app - it should exist only in real login sessions.

  ProcessType
      Omitted. The daemon declares Adaptive because it is a faceless
      worker; Sentry is a foreground app whose QoS is its own business.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>Label</key>
	<string>dev.malekswilam.macstat.xpc</string>

	<!-- Relative to Sentry.app - the app binary itself (PRODUCT_NAME
	     "Sentry", see project.yml), for the reasons in the header. -->
	<key>BundleProgram</key>
	<string>Contents/MacOS/Sentry</string>

	<!-- Must match MacStatXPCServiceName.machService exactly - the string
	     MacStatXPCClient dials and AppDelegate's listener vends. -->
	<key>MachServices</key>
	<dict>
		<key>dev.malekswilam.macstat.xpc</key>
		<true/>
	</dict>

	<!-- Attributes the Login Items entry to Sentry in System Settings,
	     same as the fan daemon's plist - the only honest presentation of
	     a background item this app installed, and the switch the user
	     flips to revoke it without deleting anything. -->
	<key>AssociatedBundleIdentifiers</key>
	<array>
		<string>dev.malekswilam.macstat</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
